  "question": "1.Real-Time Capture and Query of Medical Images: The system should be able to capture and query medical images in real time, ensuring that doctors can quickly access the required image data. The medical image information to be recorded includes Image Type, Film Time, Image Data, Image Resolution, and Image Enhancement Information. Each image corresponds to a unique patient.\n2.Record All Patient Information: The system should record all relevant information for each patient, including Name, Age, Gender, Contact Information, and Medical Records.\n3.Record All Doctor Information: The system should record all relevant information for each doctor, including Name, Department, and Contact Information. Doctors should be able to operate on images and record specific operation details, including Operation Content and Operation Time. Doctors should be able to upload images, instantly uploading the edited images and their data to the server to ensure data sharing and long-term preservation. The system should also record the Upload Time and Server Path. Each image can be shared with multiple doctors, recording the Sharing Time and Target Institution.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0166\nCREATE TABLE `patient` (\n  `patient_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `age` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `gender` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `contact_information` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `medical_records` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`patient_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `doctor` (\n  `doctor_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `department` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `contact_information` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`doctor_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `medical_image` (\n  `image_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `patient_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `image_type` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `film_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `image_data` longblob DEFAULT NULL,\n  `image_resolution` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `image_enhancement_information` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`image_id`),\n  KEY `medical_image_ibfk_1` (`patient_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `medical_image_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`patient_id`) REFERENCES `patient` (`patient_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `doctor_image_operation` (\n  `operation_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `doctor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `image_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `operation_content` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `operation_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`operation_id`),\n  KEY `doctor_image_operation_ibfk_1` (`doctor_id`),\n  KEY `doctor_image_operation_ibfk_2` (`image_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `doctor_image_operation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`doctor_id`) REFERENCES `doctor` (`doctor_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `doctor_image_operation_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`image_id`) REFERENCES `medical_image` (`image_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `image_upload` (\n  `upload_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `image_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `doctor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `upload_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `server_path` varchar(500) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`upload_id`),\n  KEY `image_upload_ibfk_1` (`image_id`),\n  KEY `image_upload_ibfk_2` (`doctor_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `image_upload_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`image_id`) REFERENCES `medical_image` (`image_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `image_upload_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`doctor_id`) REFERENCES `doctor` (`doctor_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `image_sharing` (\n  `sharing_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `image_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `doctor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sharing_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `target_institution` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`sharing_id`),\n  KEY `image_sharing_ibfk_1` (`image_id`),\n  KEY `image_sharing_ibfk_2` (`doctor_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `image_sharing_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`image_id`) REFERENCES `medical_image` (`image_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `image_sharing_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`doctor_id`) REFERENCES `doctor` (`doctor_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
